# Money's two names at the edge: a reference copy.
#
# One Caddy owns ports 80 and 443 on the studio's server, and it belongs to the
# platform: compose project selfops-edge, reading /opt/selfops/Caddyfile.edge
# from the platform's prod checkout. So the blocks below do not run from here.
# They live in the platform's Caddyfile.edge and reach it as two hotfixes of
# the platform (docs/deploy.md, "The edge"); this file is where Money keeps
# their text, and CI runs `caddy validate` on it. If the two ever differ, the
# platform's file is what the proxy reads.
#
# Two rules for a block, because a mistake in that file takes every name of
# both products away: a name goes in only once it exists in DNS, and a block
# points only at a port where something already answers.
#
# What each line is for:
#   request_body   the edge stops a body before Python sees a byte of it. 17 MB
#                  sits just above Money's own limit of 16 MiB, so the refusal
#                  a founder can meet is Money's own, as JSON.
#   reverse_proxy  the stand's loopback port. Nothing else: Money serves its
#                  page at the root itself, so the old rewrite is gone.
#   encode         Money has no web container of its own to compress a 400 KB
#                  page and a ledger of megabytes for a phone.
#   HSTS           a year, this host only. Not includeSubDomains and not
#                  preload: those are the parts that are hard to take back.
#   X-Robots-Tag   not a page for a search index, whatever it says when nobody
#                  is signed in.
#
# Not here on purpose: request buffering. It is added only after
# `caddy validate` has accepted the option on the server's own Caddy version.

# Money, the founders' ledger: a product of its own with a stack of its own
# (repository mkodzya/selfstudio-money, compose project money-prod). The
# platform neither contains nor serves it; the block is in the platform's file
# only because one Caddy owns 80 and 443. DNS for selfstudio.se is at
# Cloudflare, and the record has to be "DNS only".
finance.selfstudio.se {
	request_body {
		max_size 17MB
	}
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:5191
	encode zstd gzip
	header Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000"
	header X-Robots-Tag "noindex, nofollow"
	log {
		output stdout
		format console
	}
}

# Money's own test stand (compose project money-test): a fabricated studio,
# reseeded every night. Not the platform's test stack.
finance.test.selfstudio.se {
	request_body {
		max_size 17MB
	}
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:5192
	encode zstd gzip
	header Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000"
	header X-Robots-Tag "noindex, nofollow"
	log {
		output stdout
		format console
	}
}
